<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Korkai</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Korkai was an ancient port of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pandya-dynasty">Pandya</a> kingdom near the mouth of the Tamraparani River in modern Thoothukudi district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamil-nadu">Tamil Nadu</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. It was the centre of the pearl fisheries of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-mannar">Gulf of Mannar</a> and traded with the Roman world, and Greek writers knew it as Kolkhoi. The coastline has since moved, and the site now lies several kilometres inland.</p></div>
